# Not a build-time optimization: podman reads context files lazily per COPY, so
# a warm rebuild takes the same ~3.5s with or without this file. What it buys is
# that `.env` — real AWS credentials — and the 5 GB `.venv` stay outside the
# context, so a future broad `COPY . .` can't sweep them into the image the way
# the current selective COPY lines happen not to. RUNBOOK.md's local pipeline run
# leaves `photos/` and `jobdir/` here between rebuilds for the same reason.
#
# Patterns match paths relative to this directory and are not applied at every
# level the way .gitignore's are, so anything that can appear inside pipeline/
# needs the `**/` prefix — `__pycache__/` alone would let COPY pipeline/ ship it.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vscode/
.env
.env.*
tests/
jobdir/
photos/
